# Writing and code style

This is the public website repo. Everything here is visible to the world.

## Code comments (HTML/CSS/JS)

- No narrating what the code does. If a div has class "hero", don't comment `<!-- Hero section -->`.
- Only comment on non-obvious things: browser hacks, z-index stacking decisions, animation quirks.
- Don't add `// Initialize the app` or `// Set up event listeners` type comments.

## Copy and content

- Write like a person, not a brochure.
- Don't use marketing buzzwords: "modern", "robust", "seamless", "leverage", "streamline", "cutting-edge", "best-in-class", "next-generation", "enterprise-grade".
- Be specific about what kcore does rather than using vague superlatives.
- Short sentences. Say what it is, what it does, why someone would use it.

## Commit messages

- Lowercase, no period at the end.
- Short and direct: "fix nav links on mobile", "update hero copy", "add docs page".
- No `Type: Description` format.

## General

- Don't over-structure things.
- If something is obvious, don't explain it.
- Read it back: would a real person write this? If it sounds like a chatbot, rewrite it.
